### 8\. Preservation and security rules

Mandatory project guardrails

These rules apply to every Claude coding task and every implementation phase.

* `DATABASE_RESET=NO`.

* No `DROP TABLE`, `TRUNCATE`, database reset or destructive migrations.

* No `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd` or unrequested deletion.

* Do not recreate deleted `MASTER_PROMPT.md` or `FINAL_AUTONOMOUS_ENGINE_PROMPT.txt`.

* `MASTER_RUN_PROMPT.md` remains the source of truth if it exists.

* `PROGRESS.md` remains the progress ledger if it exists.

* Preserve `.env`, OAuth credentials, tokens and media.

* Never print secrets or commit them.

* No unapproved push, publishing, comments or uploads.

* Existing routes, endpoints, data formats and tests must remain compatible.

* Inspect before editing; list exact files to change.

* Run regression tests and verify before claiming success.

### Implementation sequence

* Phase 0 — Read-only audit

    Inspect repo, database schema, existing routes, workers, UI, tests and documentation. Create a baseline and backup plan.

* Phase 1 — Reference UI audit

    Compare public Ssemble screens and your authorized screenshots. Create screen-by-screen design and interaction specifications.

* Phase 2 — Dashboard and project UX

    Improve navigation, project cards, import workflow and job status without replacing backend logic.

* Phase 3 — AI processing and editor

    Improve transcription, clip selection, timeline, captions and reframing.

* Phase 4 — Rendering and assets

    Implement effects, music, B-roll, hooks and export.

* Phase 5 — Social integrations

    Implement OAuth and official APIs, beginning with YouTube. Keep all actual publishing disabled until tested and explicitly authorized.

* Phase 6 — Automation and analytics

    Add channel monitoring, thresholds, scheduling, post verification and performance learning.

* Phase 7 — QA and release

    Test on Android/Termux, check mobile layout, load, failures, security, data preservation and rollback.

